# The server this release line tests against.
#
# compose.yml deliberately declares no default images: a stack that silently brings up the wrong
# server produces failures that look like client bugs. Something therefore has to supply them,
# and it cannot be the caller's shell — conftest.py runs tests/data/setup_chemotion_db.sh
# directly, and that script invokes docker compose itself. This file is that something; every
# caller passes it with --env-file.
#
# IMAGES ARE PINNED BY DIGEST ON PURPOSE. Bumping a digest is a deliberate, reviewed change:
# record the new digest together with the `Version:` string that /about then reports.
#
# Pinned 2026-11-23 — ELN 3.1.4 (/about: Version: v3.1.4):
#   eln  complat/chemotion:eln-3.1.4
#   db   ptrxyz/chemotion:db-3.1.2
#
# The ELN publisher moved: 3.1.4 is `complat/chemotion`; `ptrxyz/chemotion` stops at 3.1.2.
# ComPlat published no db-3.1.4, so the DB image stays ptrxyz db-3.1.2 — the pairing ChemOrc's own
# 3.1.4 compose uses (Chemotion/ChemOrc@d1d181e, payload/docker-compose.yml).
#
# AFTER AN ELN BUMP, REMOVE THE APP VOLUME (stack down, then `docker volume rm chemotion_app_v3`).
# It holds the application code itself, and Docker fills a named volume from the image only while
# the volume is empty — a new image over an old app volume runs the old ELN, and /about says so.
#
# Superseded pins, kept so a bisect can reproduce an older run (both were unpinned tags until now):
#   until 312.1.1  eln  ptrxyz/chemotion:eln-3.1.2@sha256:784f8c4fb38f7b34789be8ba49174547b0860a5889cc5450f6acccf101c452b0  (v3.1.2)
#   until 312.1.1  db   ptrxyz/chemotion:db-3.1.2@sha256:97477d899b557b612fc84bb94ddc2b87b807d5ab5b6e405a50399d0a378b7838
CHEMOTION_ELN_IMAGE=complat/chemotion:eln-3.1.4@sha256:f9eb18e2db1ba39a7449c8b322792319bb4731957dad8ceaaec395437aaecf69
CHEMOTION_DB_IMAGE=ptrxyz/chemotion:db-3.1.2@sha256:97477d899b557b612fc84bb94ddc2b87b807d5ab5b6e405a50399d0a378b7838

# Keeps this line's containers and volumes apart from the v4 line's (volumes survive
# `docker compose down`). Up to 312.1.1 this line used the unsuffixed `chemotion_*` volumes.
CHEMOTION_STACK_SUFFIX=v3
